      ":question/id": "e3a30177-d904-5f49-bfb5-ed5c1ed92083",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{9}{x+12}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, let $u=x+12.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\text{d}x=1\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe can now rewrite the integral in terms of $u,$ solve it, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{9}{x+12}\\,\\text{d}x & =9\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot\\left(1\\,\\text{d}u\\right) \\\\ & =9\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\ & =9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+12|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
